# CoreDNS, the cluster DNS add-on (ADR 0083): built from source at the commit that tag v1.15.0 of the
# public repository is. The commit, not the tag, is the pin: the Dockerfile fetches that object and
# fails unless HEAD is it, and a tag can be moved.
#
# Why this release (chosen 2026-11-21, from the repository's tags and its GitHub releases): v1.15.0,
# published 2026-10-21, 31 days before that date, is the newest stable release.
#
# Moved by: the PM, in a pull request that reruns `make image` and `make image-repro` and the QEMU
# test of cluster DNS, when a patch release is at least two weeks old or an advisory is published for
# the pinned one. No bot proposes it.
COREDNS_REPO=https://github.com/coredns/coredns
COREDNS_VERSION=v1.15.0
COREDNS_COMMIT=a6fde3fe339c6ec848447e11cc9796be8c97b4e0
# Licences (SPDX), read from the COPYING or LICENSE of each source and checked by naru-release (ADR 0076).
COREDNS_LICENSE=Apache-2.0
